# The bulk products are BUILD OUTPUT: regenerable by build_archive.py, pinned
# byte-for-byte by MANIFEST.csv, and checked by verify_archive.py.  Versioning
# them would add ~140 MB to the repository on every rebuild for no gain.
#
# fits/ is ignored for a second reason as well: the AUTHORITATIVE copies of the
# fit records are already tracked, under finalrun/pipeline_output/chosen_visit/
# fits/*/records/ and finalrun/iue/fits/*/records/, committed on 2026-11-07
# precisely because 49 of them hold masks that exist nowhere else.  The copy
# here is derivative, so tracking it would duplicate 366 files.
spectra/
figures/
fits/

# provenance/ and code/ ARE tracked, though they too are copies.  They are small
# -- 26 files under 1 MB -- and they are SELECTIONS: which 17 of the project's 81
# scripts constitute the measurement path, and which 9 tables are hand-made
# inputs rather than derived output.  Keeping them in the repository lets someone
# browsing it see what the deposit contains without running the build.
